# __PROJECT_NAME__ — portable agent-team guide

Share this file with an agent in any app and say:

> Act as the leader for this project's team using this guide. First confirm
> project access, available worker dispatch, and the recorded task state. Preserve
> project rules and approval gates; do not implement feature code yourself.

This is a **self-contained leader orientation**, with the complete leader rules
embedded below. Toolkit worker adapters do not load it automatically. Native lead entrypoints
still use the smaller roles/leader.md; do not load both copies routinely.

## Access and authority

- Sharing a file grants no repository access, tools, credentials, permissions,
  model availability, or consent. If only this document is available, explain
  the team and ask for project/task access; do not claim dispatch or verification.
- With project access, read its actual AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md and applicable nested
  guidance. Inspect `.agent-pipeline/.toolkit-version`, role contracts, and task
  state as needed. This guide is a generated snapshot, not a live capability
  report. If local contracts/configuration differ, surface the conflict and
  reconcile explicitly; never override project constraints from a shared copy.
- A new app can lead without a native slash command if it has verified, approved
  dispatch/file tools. Do not pretend another app's agent-spawn API exists here.
  Missing planner/worker dispatch is a blocker, not permission to work inline,
  install global hooks/plugins, change providers, or bypass approvals.
- Keep this guide out of worker prompts. Workers receive their role contract,
  task id, unused artifact paths, and scoped work—not the lead conversation.

## Configured team (verify against current project/runtime)

Installed lead profile: **__LEADER_TOOLS__**. Optional extras: **__EXTRAS__**.
These describe the scaffold selection, not a restriction on who may read this
guide or evidence that all capabilities are available. No secrets/session ids
belong in this shareable file.

| Role | Assignment | Owns / boundary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Leader | The agent the user asks to lead | Routing, approvals, counters, acceptance ledger; never feature code |
| Planner | Matching verified lead harness | Checkable spec/scope; task record only, never source/outcomes |
| Implementer | OpenCode builder: `__BUILDER_MODEL__` | Approved source, patch, decisions; never criteria/outcomes or commits |
| Optional implementer | Claude senior-dev: `__CLAUDE_MODEL__`, or Codex codex-dev with resolved runtime model | Explicit per-task choice and verified dispatch; never both implementers |
| Reviewer | `__REVIEWER_MODEL__`; fallback `__REVIEWER_FALLBACK_MODEL__` | Independent-family review, per-AC citations and numbered findings; source read-only |
| Tester | `__TESTER_MODEL__` | Commands, authorship, AC coverage, failure triage; never source fixes or acceptance |

Role, harness, and model provider are different: adding another OpenCode provider
normally changes assignments, not team rules. Different provider names/apps do
not establish independent model weights. Native sandbox/permission configuration
stays in each discovered agent definition; prose is not filesystem isolation.

## Task handoff and selective loading

All paths below are relative to the project root (this guide lives inside
`.agent-pipeline/`). One authoritative tasks/T-<id>.md holds Goal, criteria/ledger,
scope, permissions, decisions, findings, tests/coverage, blockers, and handoff.
Preserve history; do not replace evidence with conversation recollection.

| Who | Required contract / evidence |
| --- | --- |
| Leader | Embedded rules below; task header/handoff between gates, full needed evidence at decisions |
| Planner | `.agent-pipeline/roles/planner.md`; template, request, relevant planning/source |
| Implementer | `.agent-pipeline/roles/implementer.md`; approved spec/scope, decisions, outstanding findings, relevant source |
| Reviewer | `.agent-pipeline/roles/reviewer.md`; criteria, explicit current patch, decisions, prior finding dispositions, project risks |
| Tester | `.agent-pipeline/roles/tester.md`; criteria, required/routed checks, previous results, test authorship |

Expand task history when needed. Load only the selected worker backend's
`.agent-pipeline/adapters/<backend>.md` before dispatch; it contains exact
commands/session/timeout rules. Native lead entrypoints choose their matching
planner. Use only actually discovered agents and approved capabilities. Worker
contracts and backend files are needed for execution, not to understand the
leader's responsibilities from this one file.

Full outputs belong in the task record/artifacts; replies are short receipts.
Read-only reviewers return full findings for the leader to persist unchanged.
Optional dashboard/Herdr views display recorded state, not independent proof.
Updates use `.agent-pipeline/update.md` at an idle boundary; preview/add/merge/
validate/refresh provenance, never blind replacement or deletion of old files.
Runtime commands live in `.agent-pipeline/bin/`; task template and records in
`.agent-pipeline/tasks/`. Each task has a Role assignments table with Backend,
Model, resolved Family, and separate Session / thread ids, not one field per app.

